Dinosaur no more


06 Jan 2021 17:20






a series a research logs and interviews follow Dr. Tera as she becomes more and more desperate to find out what killed the dinosaurs.

Seeking Greenlights:  Yes

Page Type:  SCP Article

Genre (Optional):  mystery

Page Layout (Optional):  study logs and interviews

Elevator Pitch:  XK class event/being/??? wipes most organisms from earth, causing dinosaurs to go extinct. Cause of event is the anomaly, not the death of the dinosaurs File is about how the event or item or being which is completely/mostly unknown and consists of theories of who/what the anomaly is and how to contain knowledge of the anomaly (the foundation is 100% sure of the existence of the anomaly) 

Central Narrative:  Dr. Tera is lead and sole researcher on project, even with access to virtually anything at the foundations disposal, she gets seemingly more and more frustrated with each interview and study; she eventually narrows the list down to a few theories, but either won't, shouldn't, or can't find the real answer.

Hook/Attention-Grabber:  the scp file is less about a thing (or lack thereof) and more about the research log, interview, and coverup of the scp  a opened ended conclusion leaves readers to attempt to back up their own theories.

